{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459778-extreme-situation-question-about-morality-the-old-system","id":1459778,"title":"Extreme situation question about Morality ( the old system )","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-12T15:37:38-07:00","id":1459778,"title":"Extreme situation question about Morality ( the old system )","content":"This question address the first NWoD, before the change from Morality to Integrity.<br /> <br /> So, hypotetical question.<br /> <br /> A police officer intervene in a violent situation: a raging madman, probably under drugs and alchohol influence, is taking down people with an axe. Right now is charging toward a 3 years old child and his already wounded mother.<br /> The police offficer draw is gun and shout &quot;STOP!!!&quot; as loudly as he can, to no avail. A second later ( and a second beffore the maniac's bloody axe reach the child ) he shoots, aiming for the legs, and takes down the aggressor.<br /> He immediately calls for an ambulance and provides first aid help to the wounded, including making a tourniquett for the madman.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the bullet cut the femoral artery and the madman dies before the ambulance arrives.<br /> <br /> The cop takes no pleasure in the kill and surely do not brag about it.<br /> -<br /> <br /> In this very specific circumstance, would you call for a Morality roll ( manslaughter, level 4 sin ) ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T16:05:10-07:00","id":1459783,"title":"","content":"Yep. It's certainly not Planned Murder, and the default listing doesn't really put a hard read on nonfatal violence outside the context of torture, so 4 seems an appropriate threshold for this scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T17:08:02-07:00","id":1459794,"title":"","content":"Despite the name, it is more about psychological shock than acting moral, so yes. This cop choose a course of action, it ended in death, he'll deal with the emotional baggage regardless of the action's righteousness or original intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}